# Git and push

- When you make code or doc changes in this project, **commit and push** them so the repo stays in sync with GitHub.
- Work from the **project root** (`GradePlanner`). Use:
  - `git add <paths>` or `git add .` for the changed files
  - `git commit -m "Clear, one-line message"`
  - `git push origin main` (or the current branch)
- Prefer one commit per logical change; batch small related edits into a single commit when it makes sense.
- If the user asks not to push, or Git is not available in the environment, skip the push and tell them to push manually.
- Remote is **origin** (https://github.com/kenigdav/GradePlanner). Do not change the remote URL unless the user asks.
